# @rt-category Test Scenes
# @rt-description A sphere of measured (real-world) material under a white sky: a one-bounce test of the measured BSDF.
# @rt-performance Fast
# @rt-size 2
# measured-furnace.pbrt -- a measured-BSDF sphere under a uniform white sky: a one-bounce furnace for the measured material.
#
# Every pixel is the sphere's directional albedo for the view direction, so it must be at most 1 in every channel and the same on every backend.
# It catches a path-throughput weight that is not f * |cos| / pdf: the measured material used to return the bare f on the CPU and both GPU
# backends, which put a measured sphere at 7.8 / 8.1 / 3.5 (a blue table) and 12 (a metallic one) in this furnace instead of 0.1-0.7, and a white
# paper table at 0.34 instead of 1.0, identically everywhere, so no CPU-vs-GPU comparison could see it.
# It also catches sample_f evaluating the spectra at the wrong point (u_wm instead of the luminance-warped one), which made the sampled f disagree with f().
#
# Uses synthetic-gold.bsdf (original, see measured-brdf-showroom.pbrt's header), so it carries no licence constraints.

LookAt  0 0 6    0 0 0    0 1 0
Camera "perspective" "float fov" [ 14 ]

Film "rgb" "integer xresolution" [ 32 ] "integer yresolution" [ 32 ]
Sampler "halton" "integer pixelsamples" [ 64 ]

WorldBegin

LightSource "infinite" "rgb L" [ 1 1 1 ]

Material "measured" "string filename" [ "synthetic-gold.bsdf" ]
Shape "sphere" "float radius" [ 1 ]
